# NRC-REFUSED: a neural radiance cache that cannot run on the device (its NN kernel path refused) leaves the path tracer running
# without it instead of refusing the frame (System::PathTracer::RefuseRadianceCache, PathTracer.hpp THE NEURAL RADIANCE CACHE):
# state nrc reports requested Nrc, status Off and the reason; the refusal is logged once per reason (ShaderService::
# ClaimRefusalReport for a refused shader variant); every later Nrc frame asks again, so fixing the cause takes the cache back.
Дано F:/BistroFoliageProj dnx_Night_pt, GlobalIllumination.Method PathTraced, PathTracing.Denoiser Off, PathTracing.SamplesPerPixel 64, PathTracing.PathsPerFrame 1, camera fixed on the street; machine.json ForcedNeuralKernelPath set by run Neural "Neural: Kernel path ..." to a path the device lacks (device.nn lists what it has: CoopMatFp16 on a device without cooperative matrices, Fp16 without shaderFloat16 + storageBuffer16BitAccess).
Когда PathTracing.RadianceCache Nrc; 300 frames; shoot nrc_refused; DesertCtl state nrc.
Когда PathTracing.RadianceCache Off; 300 frames; shoot off.
Тогда [nrc_refused]: state nrc: requested "Nrc", status "Off", reason names the refused kernel path and why ("the forced NN kernel path ... is refused: ..."), active false; editor.log has exactly ONE "[PathTracer] PathTracing.RadianceCache Nrc refused, the paths run without the cache (Off)" line over the 300 frames; nrc_refused is not black (mean luminance > 0) and matches off (the same 64 spp sum: RMSE(nrc_refused, off) ~ 0); 0 VUID in the log.
